<title>HONG KONG: Moody's rates Thai Ex-Im Bank $100 mln FRN A2.</title>
<headline>Moody's rates Thai Ex-Im Bank $100 mln FRN A2.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service on Wednesday said it had assigned a long-term foreign currency debt rating of A2 to the $100 million floating rate notes (FRN) due in 2000 issued by the Export-Import Bank of Thailand.  </p>
<p>Moody's said the rating reflected the close link between the bank and the Kingdom of Thailand due to its function as an instrument of government policy and economic development.</p>
<p>The Thai Ex-Im bank is 100 percent owned by Thailand through the Ministry of Finance, but is subject to the same capital and loan loss provisioning requirements stipulated by the Bank of Thailand for commercial banks, the rating agency said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6441</p>
